"make license" in each language folder:

  typescript/  npm dependencies        (license-checker-rseidelsohn)
  rust/        crates.io dependencies  (cargo-deny, rust/deny.toml)
  go/          Go modules              (go-licenses)
  python/      PyPI dependencies       (pip-licenses)
  java/        Maven dependencies      (license-maven-plugin)

Code copied or adapted from other projects is listed below with its source,
copyright and licence.

  CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md is adapted from the Contributor Covenant, version 2.1,
  https://www.contributor-covenant.org, licensed under CC BY 4.0.

  OTLP messages (all five packages). The OTLP/HTTP JSON log requests
  (ExportLogsServiceRequest) are built from the field names of the OpenTelemetry
  protocol specification and opentelemetry-proto (Copyright The OpenTelemetry
  Authors, Apache-2.0). The Python package decodes the message field of
  google.rpc.Status error bodies using the field numbers of the Google APIs
  common protos (Copyright Google LLC, Apache-2.0). No code was copied from
  these projects and no OpenObserve code or module is used; the request and
  response shapes of the OpenObserve HTTP API were taken from its public
  documentation and observed responses of the v1.1.2 container.

  Spans are exported with the official OpenTelemetry SDKs and OTLP exporters
  of each language (Apache-2.0): @opentelemetry/exporter-trace-otlp-proto,
  -otlp-http and -otlp-grpc with @grpc/grpc-js (Apache-2.0) for TypeScript;
  opentelemetry-otlp for Rust; go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp for Go;
  opentelemetry-exporter-otlp-proto-http (and the optional -proto-grpc) for
  Python; io.opentelemetry:opentelemetry-exporter-otlp for Java.

  Notable other runtime dependencies of the service code: undici (MIT) for
  TypeScript; reqwest (MIT OR Apache-2.0), base64 and percent-encoding (MIT OR
  Apache-2.0) for Rust; httpx (BSD-3-Clause) for Python; jackson-databind
  (Apache-2.0) for Java. Go uses the standard library plus OpenTelemetry.
